course: dictionary
lesson: 13207
title: Funfair
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A funfair is an outdoor show with rides, games, stalls and sweets. You pay to enjoy it, and it often travels from town to town. «We went to the funfair in town on Saturday.» The words rides, games and stalls are clues that tell you what there is to do there.
explain: In the UK and Australia, funfair is the usual word for what Americans call a carnival or a fair. «The funfair is in town all week.» If you read an American book and meet the word carnival, the idea is much the same: bright rides and sweets outdoors.
explain: Stories often use a funfair for excitement, bright lights and candyfloss. «The lights flashed as the big wheel turned.» The words flashed and turned paint a picture, even if you have never been. Use the clues around the word to picture the place.
explain: A funfair can also be a place where you need to be careful. «Mum held my hand and we agreed to meet at the big wheel if we got lost.» Stay with your adult, agree a meeting point, and follow the height rules on rides.
fact: A funfair is an outdoor show with rides, games, stalls and sweets.
fact: In the UK and Australia, «funfair» is the usual word for what Americans call a carnival or a fair.
fact: Many funfairs travel from town to town, so they come and go.
fact: Candyfloss is a sweet, fluffy treat often sold at a funfair.
fact: Before you go on a ride, follow the height rules and stay with your adult.
exercise: «The funfair is in town all week.» What is a funfair? | *An outdoor show with rides, games, stalls and sweets | A quiet park with benches | A shop that sells only clothes | A school where you learn to ride horses
exercise: «We spent our pocket money on rides and candyfloss at the funfair.» What did the children spend their money on? | A new school bag | *Rides and candyfloss | Books from the library | Train tickets home
exercise: At the funfair, one ride costs 3 tokens. How many tokens do two rides cost? | 9 | *6 | 4 | 5
test: «Mum said, "Stay with me and we will meet at the big wheel."» Why is this good advice at a funfair? | It makes the rides cost more | It stops the music | It means you can wander off alone | *It keeps you safe if you get lost
test: In «The funfair is in town», what does in town mean? | It has been closed for years | *It has come to your town for a while | It is far away in another country | It is inside a building
exam: In the USA, what do people often call a funfair? | A library | A harbour | *A carnival | A museum
